{"id":"wikipedia-languages","title":"Languages with the most Wikipedia articles","prompt":"Name the 10 languages whose Wikipedia has the most articles","noun":"languages","category":"Oddball","metric":"Articles in that language's Wikipedia","blitz":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: List of Wikipedias","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Wikipedias","asOf":"2026-11-20","dataAsOf":"November 2026"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"English","aliases":["English Wikipedia","English language","English languge","Englishlanguage","Saozneg","Anglesc"],"value":"7,266,830 articles","n":7266830,"article":"English language","fact":{"text":"The first edition, started on 15 January 2001; it held over half of all Wikipedia articles in 2003, and 10.6% now.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_Wikipedia"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Cebuano","aliases":["Cebuano Wikipedia","Cebuano language","Sugbuanon","Sugboanon","Sebuano","Sebuano language","Sinugboanong Binisaya","Sinugboanon","Cabuano language","Cebuan language","Southern Kana dialect","Northern Kana dialect","Kana dialect","Leyteño language","Leyteño dialect","Davaoeño dialect","Cebuan dialect","Cebú language","Standard Cebuan","Sugbuanon language","Sugbuano language","Sinugbuanong Binisayâ","Sinebwano","Bisaya","Binisaya"],"value":"6,116,386 articles","n":6116386,"article":"Cebuano language","fact":{"text":"A language of the Philippines; nearly all of its Wikipedia's articles were made by bots, mostly Lsjbot, and it has under 200 active users.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cebuano_Wikipedia"}},{"rank":3,"name":"German","aliases":["German Wikipedia","German language","Deutsche Sprache","Deutsche language","Deutsch language","Deutsch","Deutsche"],"value":"3,167,674 articles","n":3167674,"article":"German language","fact":{"text":"The second-oldest edition (March 2001), and in 2009 the second to pass a million articles, after English.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_Wikipedia"}},{"rank":4,"name":"